  "body": "## What changed\n\nParameter patch refusals now name merged field paths and keys when a shape change retains the old key.\nBoth add_operation and edit_operation use the shared diagnostic.\nNested fields include links.approach.lead_out.\nThe MCP skill explains how to remove the old key with null in the same patch.\n\n## Cause\n\nJSON merge patch keeps object keys that the caller does not remove.\nA patch that adds arc to a linear lead produces both keys.\nThe enum parser refuses that object but previously gave no field or shape names.\nThe fix keeps this refusal and adds context from objects that expanded from one key to several keys.\nIt preserves the original parser error.\nIt does not treat every object with one key as an enum.\n\n## Tests\n\nBase: upstream/main 0510ff382.\nReadings: shared MCP patch parser, project parameter serialization, and the existing MCP integration fixture.\n\n- add_contour_lead_shape_refusal_names_retained_shapes\n- edit_contour_lead_shape_refusal_preserves_parameters_and_undo\n- nested_lead_out_shape_refusal_names_full_parameter_path\n\nAll three pins fail on unchanged code and pass with the fix.\nThey check field paths, both shapes, null removal, and valid replacement.\nThey also check unchanged parameters, undo history, and edits within one shape.\nMutation: replace edit.rs with upstream/main, then run all three pins. All three fail.\nRestore the fix, then run all three pins. All three pass.\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passes all 17 steps.\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings passes.\nEach diff hunk has a written justification. The decision is in docs/decisions/2876-enum-patch-diagnostic.md.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. git diff --stat upstream/main -- '*.nc' '*.cl' is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nGUI, release heavy lanes, and a physical machine were not exercised.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2773 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes set_stock in edit.rs. This PR changes patched and adds merged_key_context.\nPRs #2773, #2799, #2716, and #2678 touch the same MCP skill file in different entries; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThis PR adds the lead shape entry beside edit_operation.\nNo stack is needed.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: MCP parameter patch refusals name retained shape keys and nested fields and explain null removal.\n\nFixes #2876\n",
